 inside the crest of the pulse"}],"hatch":[],"settings":"$\\phi = 0$, $z = 0$","input":"The pulse of Weber, Wheeler, and Bonnor, of width $a$: $\\psi = \\sqrt{2}\\,C\\sqrt{D_+ + a^2 + \\rho^2 - c^2t^2}/D_+$ and $\\gamma = \\tfrac{C^2}{2a^2}\\left(1 - 2a^2\\rho^2D_-^2/D_+^4 + (\\rho^2 - a^2 - c^2t^2)/D_+\\right)$, with $D_\\pm^2 = (a^2 + \\rho^2 - c^2t^2)^2 \\pm 4a^2c^2t^2$, at $C = a$, checked to solve this spacetime's own field equations.","caption":["The same plane in the null chart, $u$ and $v$ ($\\phi = 0$, $z = 0$), drawn against $(v - u)/2 = \\rho$ and $(u + v)/2 = ct$. Only $g_{uv}$ is nonzero on it, so a null direction has $du\\,dv = 0$, and the light rays are the coordinate lines $u = $ const and $v = $ const themselves, for every wave.","The pulse comes in with its crest just outside the ray $v = 0$, is greatest on the axis at $u = v = 0$, and goes out with its crest just outside $u = 0$."],"source":{"fields":["coords","parameters","metric_components","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","domains"],"version":"d1ce0a59b8c615ce"},"slices":[{"view":"pulse","surface":0,"label":"$ct = 1\\,a$","version":"4a6b34c63e57225c","lines":[[[0.0,0.2],[1.0,0.2]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[1.0,0.2],"anchor":"br","dx":0,"dy":-1.3}},{"view":"pulse","surface":1,"label":"$ct = 2\\,a$","version":"bed4b321a37f9849","lines":[[[0.0,0.3],[1.0,0.3]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[1.0,0.3],"anchor":"br","dx":0,"dy":-1.3}},{"view":"pulse","surface":2,"label":"$ct = 4\\,a$","version":"d814c41f064b8626","lines":[[[0.0,0.5],[1.0,0.5]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[1.0,0.5],"anchor":"br","dx":0,"dy":-1.3}},{"view":"pulse","surface":3,"label":"$ct = 8\\,a$","version":"8f1193d4ff5eebad","lines":[[[0.0,0.9],[1.0,0.9]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[1.0,0.9],"anchor":"br","dx":0,"dy":-1.3}}]}]}}
